---
const lanes = [
  { name: "Auto-merge", who: "What your rules allow, from an agent with 10 merged changes and no recent incident", chips: ["Docs, by your rule", "Internal changes your policy lists"] },
  { name: "Judge", who: "The default: verified on evidence before it merges", chips: ["Everything no rule or floor moves"] },
  { name: "A person", who: "Sensitive code, security and the rules of the game", chips: ["Auth, payments, personal data", "Tests, CI and policy", "Anything outside the stated intent"], signal: true },
  { name: "Blocked", who: "Until someone fixes it or approves it", chips: ["A committed secret", "Writes outside the task's scope", "Weakened tests, unapproved"], blocked: true },
];
---

<section class="chapter" id="lanes" data-phase="4" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapter-copy">
      <h2 class="display-l" id="lanes-title">Every change gets a lane.</h2>
      <p class="body-l">
        Each change is routed by the rows of its report. Routine work merges on evidence alone, the judge takes the
        middle, risky changes go to a person, and some never merge as they are.
      </p>
      <ul class="lanes">
        {
          lanes.map((l) => (
            <li class="o-lane glass">
              <span class="o-lane__name">{l.name}</span>
              <span class="o-lane__who">{l.who}</span>
              {l.chips.map((c) => (
                <span class:list={["o-chip", l.signal && "o-chip--signal", l.blocked && "o-chip--blocked"]}>{c}</span>
              ))}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="body muted">
        You write the rules in <code class="code">onus.yaml</code>. Floors no rule can lower keep risky changes with
        people, and a learned model can only move a change up a lane, never down.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lanes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .lanes .o-lane {
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .lanes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
